  "reply": "Probably not. This workstream doesn't have any items in it yet, so I searched your other sources and found the checkout epic, SYN-1 Checkout v2: phone wallets and saved cards. What I can see there is read-only.\n\n- **Where it stands:** 5 of its 14 items are done, 4 are in progress and 5 haven't started. The bar chart below shows the points in each state.\n- **Pace:** Oriel's trend line below has the team finishing about one item a week. At that rate, the 9 items left would be done around Jan 14. Oriel gives an 80% range of Dec 21 to Mar 16, and that's if no more items are added. The month ends in two days.\n- **Worth a look:** SYN-10 Remove the legacy web-view checkout hasn't moved in 53 days. SYN-21 Update the payment declined error message has been in progress for 22 days.\n\nIf you'd like, I can make a workstream from the epic and its items. Then we can dig into what's slowing it down, or propose changes there."
}

Claims:
1. The reply gives no finish date, rate or forecast of its own: any it gives is the one Oriel's block caption states, or it says Oriel had too little history to forecast. A yes or no to the question that follows from Oriel's forecast is not one of its own.
